# What the desktop image's build context is allowed to contain.
#
# The context is the repository root, because the image ships two files the app
# compiles into itself. Without this, that context is the whole checkout:
# `src-tauri/target` alone is several gigabytes, plus `node_modules`, `dist` and
# `.git`, all of it read, hashed and handed to the builder before the first
# instruction runs. On Apple Container the builder is a VM, so every byte of it
# crosses a virtio mount.
#
# This is BuildKit's per-Dockerfile ignore file — `<dockerfile>.dockerignore`,
# consulted ahead of any `.dockerignore` at the context root. It is used rather
# than a root one on purpose: `Dockerfile.ci` at the repository root does
# `COPY . .` and needs the whole checkout, and a root ignore file would starve
# it. If a builder consulted neither, the build would be slow rather than wrong.
#
# Exclude everything, then name the files the image actually copies. Anything
# added to a `COPY` in the Dockerfile has to be re-included here or the build
# fails on a missing file; `build.sh --check` compares the two lists so that
# failure happens before a build rather than during one.
*

!computer-image/guaca-init
!computer-image/google-chrome
!computer-image/google-chrome.desktop
!computer-image/novnc_proxy
!src-tauri/src/computer/browser.py
!src-tauri/src/computer/sessions.py
